The Sleeping Beauty problem:
- On Sunday, Beauty is put to sleep. A fair coin is flipped.
- If Heads: Beauty is awakened on Monday, interviewed, then the experiment ends.
- If Tails: Beauty is awakened on Monday, interviewed, put back to sleep with amnesia, awakened on Tuesday, interviewed again, then the experiment ends.
- Each awakening: Beauty is asked "What is your credence that the coin landed Heads?"

The 1/2 position: The coin is fair, so P(Heads) = 1/2. No new relevant information is acquired upon awakening.
The 1/3 position: Upon awakening, there are three possible awakening events (Heads-Monday, Tails-Monday, Tails-Tuesday), equally likely from Beauty's perspective, so P(Heads) = 1/3.

